// RtOp, gpu: The GPU. Read by `compiler/kir/build.rs`.
/// `list.map(f)` on the GPU (spec 15.2): the list, the closure and the
/// kernel's WGSL; gives the new list, or `none` for the CPU to do it.
GpuMap,
/// With `KAVACH_GPU=check`: the CPU's list from a `map` the GPU also
/// ran, compared with the GPU's; gives the CPU's list.
GpuCheck,
/// `GpuMap` whose result may stay in GPU memory only: every read of
/// it is a `GpuFetch` first (`gpu_stay.rs`).
GpuMapStay,
/// A list, with its items brought back from GPU memory if a
/// `GpuMapStay` left them only there.
GpuFetch,
/// `list.sum(f)` of `Int32` or `UInt32` on the GPU (spec 15.2): the
/// list, the closure and the kernel's WGSL; gives the sum when
/// `GpuReduced` says the GPU did it.
GpuSum,
/// `list.min()` on the GPU: the list, a placeholder and the kernel.
GpuMin,
/// `list.max()` on the GPU, as `GpuMin`.
GpuMax,
/// Whether the last `GpuSum`, `GpuMin` or `GpuMax` gave its value; if
/// not, the CPU works it out, in order.
GpuReduced,
/// A `GpuSum`, `GpuMin` or `GpuMax` that doesn't wait (`gpu_later.rs`):
/// its value comes through the `GpuLaterNext` after it.
GpuSumLater,
GpuMinLater,
GpuMaxLater,
/// A new queue of reductions that didn't wait.
GpuLaterNew,
/// Adds the reduction just made to queue `a`, and gives whether one is
/// due, which its statement then runs for: the oldest, when too many
/// are under way or the CPU must do the newest, or when `b` is 1 and
/// any is left.
GpuLaterNext,
/// The value of the reduction `GpuLaterNext` gave; `GpuReduced` says
/// whether it has one.
GpuLaterValue,
/// Its list, for the CPU to work it out when it has no value.
GpuLaterList,
/// `list.filter(f)` on the GPU (spec 15.2): the list, the closure and
/// the kernel's WGSL; gives the new list, or `none` for the CPU to do
/// it.
GpuFilter,
/// `GpuFilter` whose result may stay in GPU memory only, as
/// `GpuMapStay`.
GpuFilterStay,
/// `xs[a:b:step]` of a list in a program with GPU `map`s (spec 15.4):
/// the list and the slice's words, as `ListSlicePart`. Made on the GPU
/// when the list's items are only in GPU memory, else on the CPU.
GpuSlice,
/// `GpuSlice` whose result may stay in GPU memory only, as
/// `GpuMapStay`: made on the GPU whenever the list's items are there.
GpuSliceStay,
/// At the start of a program with GPU kernels: open the GPU and
/// compile the kernels (its text, joined by `\0`) on a background
/// thread, while the program does its first work.
GpuWarm,
/// Drawing in a window (spec 14.24, `runtime/native/src/rt_draw.rs`), by
/// number: a screen on window `a` (can fail), the screen's next frame
/// (`a` the screen, `b` its window; can fail), clearing frame `a` to the
/// colors in list `b`, showing it, letting it go, and closing a screen.
DrawScreen,
DrawFrame,
DrawClear,
DrawShow,
DrawDropFrame,
DrawClose,
/// `gpu.pipeline(v, f)`: the vertex and fragment fns, and their WGSL.
DrawPipeline,
/// A frame's draw: the frame, the pipeline, and (vertices, instances,
/// shared value, textures).
DrawDraw,
/// A texture (spec 15.3): `a` wide, `b` high, the pixels in list `c`
/// (can fail); and letting texture `a` go.
DrawTexture,
DrawDropTexture,
/// `on gpu(n) x`, `gpu.on(d) { … }` and `xs.map(f, on: d)` (spec 15.6):
/// puts a place on the task's scope stack with GPU work on device `a`,
/// and gives its depth, as `ScopePlace`; a device the machine doesn't
/// have is a panic.
GpuPlace,
/// At the program's start (spec 15.6): `a`, the highest GPU number
/// written in the code (`gpu(n) fn`, `on gpu(n)`), or -1; `b`, the text
/// of `[run] gpu`. A device that isn't there stops the program.
GpuStart,
/// Drawing for user interfaces (spec 14.24.1): a canvas (`a` the list of
/// width, height and samples, owned; can fail), its pixels as bytes, its
/// texture (`b` 1 for nearest); a frame's state (`a` the frame, `b`
/// which part, `c` the values, owned); and part of texture `a` changed
/// (`b` the area, `c` the pixels, both owned).
DrawCanvas,
DrawCanvasPixels,
DrawCanvasTexture,
DrawState,
DrawUpdate,
